arch=arm64
vmlinux_btf=6.12 kernel BTF dump (bpftool btf dump file <BTF copied from /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux> format c, Amazon Linux 2023 aarch64, 6.12.113-138.209.amzn2023.aarch64)
clang=Ubuntu clang version 18.1.3 (1ubuntu1)
load_verified=bpftool prog loadall, Amazon Linux 2023 aarch64 (6.12.113-138.209.amzn2023.aarch64, QEMU-emulated), all 14 programs pinned
notes=rebuilt because include/rt_event_contract.h changed (a comment only);
  bpf/rt_file.bpf.c is unchanged, and the object has the same 8 program
  sections and 14 programs as the one it replaces. The header moved from 6.8
  to 6.12. Its struct renamedata still has new_dir and no new_parent, so
  compiling against it keeps exercising the bpf_core_field_exists() fallback
  path that the x86 object's 7.0 header cannot reach. CO-RE resolves field
  offsets against the kernel the object is loaded on, not the header.
